<%- include('partials/header') %>

<div class="page-title-section fade-in-up">
    <h1>SIP (Systematic Investment Plan) Calculator</h1>
    <p>Calculate the estimated future returns on your monthly mutual fund investments with compounding, inflation adjustments, and PDF statements.</p>
</div>

<div class="form-card fade-in-up">

    <div class="row g-5">
        <!-- Left Column: Inputs -->
        <div class="col-lg-7">
            <!-- Monthly Investment -->
            <div class="slider-container">
                <div class="row align-items-center">
                    <div class="col-md-5">
                        <label for="monthlyInput" class="form-label mb-0 fw-bold">Monthly Investment</label>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-7">
                        <div class="input-group">
                            <span class="input-group-text">₹</span>
                            <input type="number" class="form-control" id="monthlyInput" min="500" max="1000000" step="500" placeholder="e.g., 10,000">
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div id="monthlyWords" class="number-words-preview"></div>
                <input type="range" min="500" max="200000" step="500" class="form-range mt-2" id="monthlySlider">
                <div id="monthlyPresets"></div>
            </div>

            <!-- Expected Return Rate -->
            <div class="slider-container">
                <div class="row align-items-center">
                    <div class="col-md-5">
                        <label for="rateInput" class="form-label mb-0 fw-bold">Expected Return Rate</label>
                        <small class="d-block text-muted" style="font-size:0.75rem;">(Nifty 50 avg: ~12-14%)</small>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-7">
                        <div class="input-group">
                            <input type="number" class="form-control" id="rateInput" min="1" max="30" step="0.5" placeholder="e.g., 12">
                            <span class="input-group-text">% p.a.</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <input type="range" min="1" max="30" step="0.5" class="form-range mt-2" id="rateSlider">
                <div id="ratePresets"></div>
            </div>

            <!-- Time Period -->
            <div class="slider-container">
                <div class="row align-items-center">
                    <div class="col-md-5">
                        <label class="form-label mb-0 fw-bold">Time Period</label>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-7">
                        <div class="btn-group w-100" role="group">
                            <input type="radio" class="btn-check" name="periodType" id="periodTypeYears" autocomplete="off" checked>
                            <label class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" for="periodTypeYears">Years</label>
                            <input type="radio" class="btn-check" name="periodType" id="periodTypeMonths" autocomplete="off">
                            <label class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" for="periodTypeMonths">Months</label>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="input-group mt-2">
                    <input type="number" class="form-control" id="periodInput" min="1" max="40" step="1" placeholder="e.g., 15">
                    <span class="input-group-text" id="periodUnitLabel">Years</span>
                </div>
                <input type="range" min="1" max="40" step="1" class="form-range mt-2" id="periodSlider">
                <div id="periodPresets"></div>
            </div>

            <!-- Inflation Adjustment Toggle -->
            <div class="form-check form-switch mt-3 p-3 rounded" style="background: var(--bg-input); border: 1px solid var(--border);">
                <input class="form-check-input ms-0 me-3" type="checkbox" id="inflationToggle" style="cursor: pointer;">
                <label class="form-check-label fw-semibold" for="inflationToggle" style="cursor: pointer;">
                    🔥 Adjust for Inflation (6% p.a. Purchasing Power)
                </label>
                <small class="d-block text-muted mt-1" style="font-size:0.75rem;">Calculates what your future wealth will actually buy in today's money value.</small>
            </div>
        </div>
        
        <!-- Right Column: Results -->
        <div class="col-lg-5 d-flex flex-column">
            <div id="initialState" class="d-flex flex-grow-1 align-items-center justify-content-center h-100 text-center text-muted p-4" style="background-color: var(--bg-input); border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid var(--border);">
                <h4>Enter your investment details to see the future value.</h4>
            </div>

            <div id="resultsState" class="flex-grow-1" style="display: none;">
                <div class="emi-result-display mb-3">
                    <div class="label">Estimated Future Value</div>
                    <div class="amount" id="futureValue">₹0</div>
                    <div id="inflationAdjustedBadge" class="mt-2 text-warning fw-semibold" style="display:none; font-size:0.9rem;">
                        Real Purchasing Power Today: <strong id="realValueText">₹0</strong>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="emi-summary-card">
                    <div class="summary-item">
                        <div>
                            <span class="dot" style="background-color: #0d6efd;"></span>
                            <span class="label">Invested Amount</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="value" id="investedAmount">₹0</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="summary-item">
                        <div>
                            <span class="dot" style="background-color: #10b981;"></span>
                            <span class="label">Est. Returns</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="value" id="estimatedReturns" style="color: #10b981;">₹0</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="summary-item">
                        <div>
                            <span class="dot" style="background-color: #f59e0b;"></span>
                            <span class="label">Wealth Multiplier</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="value" id="wealthMultiplier">1.0x</div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center mt-3" style="max-height: 220px;">
                    <canvas id="sipPieChart"></canvas>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Action Toolbar: PDF, CSV, Share, Save -->
    <div class="action-toolbar" id="sipActionToolbar" style="display: none;">
        <span class="toolbar-label">Tools & Export:</span>
        <button type="button" class="btn-action-tool" id="btnExportPDF">
            <span>📄</span> Download PDF Report
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-action-tool" id="btnExportCSV">
            <span>📊</span> Export Excel/CSV
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-action-tool btn-whatsapp" id="btnShareWA">
            <span>💬</span> Share on WhatsApp
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-action-tool" id="btnCopyLink">
            <span>🔗</span> Copy Link
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-action-tool" id="btnSaveCalc">
            <span>💾</span> Save Calculation
        </button>
    </div>
    
    <!-- Yearly/Monthly Breakdown -->
    <div id="yearlyBreakdownSection" class="mt-5" style="display: none;">
        <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center mb-3">
            <h4 class="m-0" id="projectionTitle">Year-by-Year Wealth Growth</h4>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-warning" onclick="exportTableToCSV('sip_schedule', 'projectionTable')">
                📥 Download CSV Table
            </button>
        </div>
        <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-striped table-bordered text-center" id="projectionTable">
                <thead class="table-dark" id="projectionHead"></thead>
                <tbody id="projectionBody"></tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Related Calculators Section -->
    <div class="related-calculators-section">
        <h5 class="related-calc-title">💡 Explore Related Calculators</h5>
        <div class="row g-3">
            <div class="col-md-3 col-6">
                <a href="/step-up-sip-calculator" class="related-mini-card">
                    <span class="icon">🚀</span>
                    <div>
                        <div class="title">Step-Up SIP</div>
                        <div class="desc">Add yearly 10% hike</div>
                    </div>
                </a>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-3 col-6">
                <a href="/compound-interest" class="related-mini-card">
                    <span class="icon">📈</span>
                    <div>
                        <div class="title">Compound Interest</div>
                        <div class="desc">Lump sum growth</div>
                    </div>
                </a>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-3 col-6">
                <a href="/ppf-calculator" class="related-mini-card">
                    <span class="icon">🏛️</span>
                    <div>
                        <div class="title">PPF Calculator</div>
                        <div class="desc">100% Tax-Free safe</div>
                    </div>
                </a>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-3 col-6">
                <a href="/retirement-calculator" class="related-mini-card">
                    <span class="icon">🌅</span>
                    <div>
                        <div class="title">Retirement Corpus</div>
                        <div class="desc">Plan early retirement</div>
                    </div>
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Guide, AEO Definitions, Comparison Table & SEO Accordion -->
    <div class="info-accordion mt-5">
        <!-- E-E-A-T Authority & Editorial Trust Card -->
        <div class="p-3 mb-4 rounded-3 border" style="background: rgba(13, 110, 253, 0.05); border-color: rgba(13, 110, 253, 0.2) !important;">
            <div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center justify-content-between gap-2">
                <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
                    <span style="font-size: 1.3rem;">🛡️</span>
                    <div>
                        <strong class="text-body-emphasis small d-block">Verified Financial Calculation Engine</strong>
                        <span class="text-muted" style="font-size: 0.78rem;">Calculations verified as per SEBI & AMFI mutual fund guidelines for FY 2026-27. Last reviewed: November 2026.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <span class="badge bg-success-subtle text-success border border-success-subtle px-2.5 py-1 rounded-pill" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">✓ Fact-Checked & Private</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- AEO Quick Definition Box (Targeted for Google AI Overviews & Featured Snippets) -->
        <div class="card p-4 rounded-4 mb-4 border" style="background: var(--bg-card, #0f172a);">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold mb-3" style="color: var(--heading-color, #f8fafc);">What is a Systematic Investment Plan (SIP)?</h2>
            <p class="lead mb-3 text-secondary" style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.7;">
                A <strong>Systematic Investment Plan (SIP)</strong> is an investment vehicle offered by mutual fund houses (AMCs) that allows an individual to invest a predetermined fixed sum of money at regular intervals (monthly, weekly, or quarterly) into a chosen mutual fund scheme instead of making a lump-sum commitment.
            </p>
            <p class="text-muted small mb-0">
                By investing through SIP, investors benefit from <strong>Rupee Cost Averaging</strong> (accumulating more fund units during market dips) and the <strong>Power of Compounding</strong>, making it one of the most disciplined and effective strategies to build long-term generational wealth.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Mathematical Formula Breakdown -->
        <div class="card p-4 rounded-4 mb-4 border" style="background: var(--bg-card, #0f172a);">
            <h3 class="h5 fw-bold mb-2" style="color: var(--heading-color, #f8fafc);">📐 SIP Compound Growth Mathematical Formula</h3>
            <p class="small text-muted mb-3">Our SIP calculator applies the industry-standard actuarial formula used by asset management companies:</p>
            <div class="p-3 rounded-3 font-monospace fw-bold text-primary mb-3 text-center" style="background: rgba(13,110,253,0.08); font-size: 1.1rem; overflow-x: auto;">
                M = P × [ (1 + i)ⁿ - 1 ] / i × (1 + i)
            </div>
            <div class="row g-2 small text-muted">
                <div class="col-md-6"><strong>M:</strong> Maturity wealth accumulated at the end of the tenure.</div>
                <div class="col-md-6"><strong>P:</strong> Amount invested each month (Monthly SIP contribution).</div>
                <div class="col-md-6"><strong>i:</strong> Periodic rate of interest (Annual return % / 12 / 100).</div>
                <div class="col-md-6"><strong>n:</strong> Total number of compounding monthly payments (Years × 12).</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Comparison Table: SIP vs Lumpsum vs Bank FD -->
        <div class="card p-4 rounded-4 mb-4 border" style="background: var(--bg-card, #0f172a);">
            <h3 class="h5 fw-bold mb-3" style="color: var(--heading-color, #f8fafc);">📊 Comparison: SIP vs Lumpsum vs Bank Fixed Deposit (FD)</h3>
            <div class="table-responsive">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover align-middle mb-0 text-center" style="font-size: 0.85rem;">
                    <thead class="table-light">
                        <tr>
                            <th class="text-start">Feature</th>
                            <th>Monthly SIP</th>
                            <th>Lumpsum Mutual Fund</th>
                            <th>Bank Fixed Deposit (FD)</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody class="text-muted">
                        <tr>
                            <td class="text-start fw-semibold text-body-emphasis">Investment Frequency</td>
                            <td>Monthly (₹500+)</td>
                            <td>One-time upfront</td>
                            <td>One-time upfront</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="text-start fw-semibold text-body-emphasis">Historical Return (CAGR)</td>
                            <td>12% - 15% (Equity)</td>
                            <td>12% - 15% (Equity)</td>
                            <td>6.5% - 7.5% (Guaranteed)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="text-start fw-semibold text-body-emphasis">Market Timing Risk</td>
                            <td>Very Low (Rupee Cost Averaging)</td>
                            <td>High (Entry point matters)</td>
                            <td>Zero Market Risk</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="text-start fw-semibold text-body-emphasis">Inflation Protection</td>
                            <td>High (Beats 6% inflation)</td>
                            <td>High (Beats 6% inflation)</td>
                            <td>Negative / Low Real Return</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="text-start fw-semibold text-body-emphasis">Taxation (FY 2026-27)</td>
                            <td>12.5% LTCG above ₹1.25L</td>
                            <td>12.5% LTCG above ₹1.25L</td>
                            <td>Taxed at slab rates (up to 30%)</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Mutual Fund Capital Gains Tax Rules (FY 2026-27) -->
        <div class="card p-4 rounded-4 mb-4 border" style="background: var(--bg-card, #0f172a);">
            <h3 class="h5 fw-bold mb-2" style="color: var(--heading-color, #f8fafc);">🧾 Mutual Fund Taxation Rules (FY 2026-27 / AY 2027-28)</h3>
            <p class="small text-muted mb-3">Under the updated Income Tax rules, capital gains from mutual fund SIP redemptions are taxed on a First-In-First-Out (FIFO) basis:</p>
            <div class="row g-3 small">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="p-3 rounded-3 border h-100" style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02);">
                        <strong class="text-primary d-block mb-1">Long-Term Capital Gains (LTCG):</strong>
                        <p class="text-muted mb-0">For equity mutual fund units held for <strong>more than 12 months</strong>, profits exceeding <strong>₹1.25 Lakh per financial year</strong> are taxed at a flat rate of <strong>12.5%</strong> (without indexation benefit).</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="p-3 rounded-3 border h-100" style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02);">
                        <strong class="text-warning d-block mb-1">Short-Term Capital Gains (STCG):</strong>
                        <p class="text-muted mb-0">For equity units redeemed <strong>within 12 months</strong> from the date of investment, profits are taxed at a flat rate of <strong>20%</strong>.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- FAQ Accordion Section -->
        <h3 class="h4 fw-bold mt-5 mb-3" style="color: var(--heading-color, #f8fafc);">❓ Frequently Asked Questions (SIP FAQs)</h3>
        <div class="accordion" id="calculatorInfoAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h4 class="accordion-header" id="headingOne">
                    <button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseOne" aria-expanded="true">
                        How does the SIP calculator determine future investment value?
                    </button>
                </h4>
                <div id="collapseOne" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
                    <div class="accordion-body text-muted">
                        The calculator uses the compound interest formula for annuities: <code>M = P × [ (1 + i)ⁿ - 1 ] / i × (1 + i)</code>. It computes monthly returns compounded on both your monthly contributions and prior accumulated profits, delivering accurate maturity wealth estimates.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h4 class="accordion-header" id="headingTwo">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseTwo">
                        What is a realistic expected rate of return for equity SIP in India?
                    </button>
                </h4>
                <div id="collapseTwo" class="accordion-collapse collapse">
                    <div class="accordion-body text-muted">
                        Historically, broad market indices like the Nifty 50 and BSE Sensex have delivered a CAGR between <strong>12% and 14%</strong> over rolling 10 to 15-year horizons. For mid-cap and small-cap funds, returns have ranged between 14% and 17%, though with higher short-term volatility. A conservative planning benchmark of <strong>12% p.a.</strong> is widely recommended.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h4 class="accordion-header" id="headingThree">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseThree">
                        What happens if I miss a monthly SIP installment?
                    </button>
                </h4>
                <div id="collapseThree" class="accordion-collapse collapse">
                    <div class="accordion-body text-muted">
                        Mutual fund companies (AMCs) do not levy any penalties if you miss an installment due to insufficient bank balance. Your existing units continue to earn returns and compound. However, your bank might charge an ECS / NACH auto-debit bounce fee. If you miss 3 consecutive debits, the AMC may pause the SIP.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h4 class="accordion-header" id="headingFour">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseFour">
                        How does inflation adjustment change the real value of my future wealth?
                    </button>
                </h4>
                <div id="collapseFour" class="accordion-collapse collapse">
                    <div class="accordion-body text-muted">
                        Inflation diminishes purchasing power over time. When you enable the <em>"🔥 Adjust for Inflation"</em> toggle in this calculator (factoring in an average 6% annual inflation rate), it calculates what your nominal maturity wealth will actually be worth in today’s rupees, helping you plan realistic retirement and education targets.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h4 class="accordion-header" id="headingFive">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseFive">
                        What is a Step-Up SIP and why is it better than a regular SIP?
                    </button>
                </h4>
                <div id="collapseFive" class="accordion-collapse collapse">
                    <div class="accordion-body text-muted">
                        A Step-Up (or Top-Up) SIP automatically increases your monthly investment by a fixed percentage (e.g. 10% each year) in tandem with annual salary increments. Over a 15-year period, a 10% annual step-up can nearly <strong>double your final accumulated corpus</strong> compared to a static flat SIP. Try our <a href="/step-up-sip-calculator" class="text-primary fw-semibold">Step-Up SIP Calculator</a> to compare numbers.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Embedded FAQPage JSON-LD for Google Rich Snippets -->
        <script type="application/ld+json">
        {
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
